From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:00:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] keybindings: Capture a mouse button under Caminito

Under Caminito a System shortcut can be a mouse button as well as a key,
written where a keysym's name would be, as "Button" and X's number for
it: "<Super>Button8". While a row captures, a press of the middle
button, or of a side button, alone or with modifiers, or of the left or
right button with a modifier, becomes the row's shortcut. A bare left
or right click goes to the list as before, so a click outside the row
still ends the capture, and the wheel is never a shortcut.

The keyboard is grabbed on its own before the rest of the seat, since
that's the grab GDK holds a shortcuts inhibitor for on Wayland, and
with one Caminito gives the dialog the presses it would otherwise take.

A row shows a button as Caminito's Window menu does, "Super+Back
Button", in English and in Spanish. A bare middle button asks first,
since it ends middle-click paste, and so does a click that
mouse-button-modifier takes over a window. A button another row has
gets the question a key gets.

Under Marco the dialog captures keys alone, as stock, and a row whose
value names a button shows as disabled, with its value kept until the
row is set.
